  "repeats": [],
  "notes": [
   "The page has no pin table and its schematic image did not load. Connections follow the standard Debounce circuit: 5V to one side of the button, the other side to digital pin 2, and a 10k pull-down from that side to GND.",
   "The sketch uses pin 2 for the button, so the teal wire goes to pin 2.",
   "The step 1 parts are unchanged, apart from wire4's colour. Wire4 is the short jumper that carries 5V from the + rail to the button's top side. I changed it from black to red because it carries 5V.",
   "The exact breadboard holes are my choice. The button straddles the centre gap in columns 10 and 11. The bottom half (columns 10 and 11) is the input side, with the signal wire and pull-down resistor in column 10. The top half is the 5V side, with 5V fed to column 11 by wire4.",
   "Power and ground go to the bottom rails (bp, bn), as the image shows."
  ]
 },
